<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    The Choir of the Spire (docs/design/peoples-third.md, the seventh of the eight; docs/design/peoples.md, "Release G";
    Source/ColonyCouncil/Peoples/PeoplesG2.cs): a people living in the shadow of an archotech spire, changed by it over
    generations, calm, kind and unsettling. Beyond spacer by the design; in Rimfolk's ages that is the spacer age with the
    archotech's flavour (techLevel Spacer, ageLimit 3). They arise in every age (ariseAges 0~3: the Spire was there before
    any of the ages). Their technology is beyond anything else in the region, and they barely use it. The look: pale robes
    in spire lilac, everyone the same pale and nothing else alike, and no armour at all; their cantors with Royalty the
    eltex of the psychic. Most are psycasters (Royalty; Vanilla Psycasts Expanded's Harmonist, Empath, Archotechist,
    Protector, Puppeteer and Staticlord paths), A RimWorld of Magic's bards and psionics among them, archite genes with
    Biotech; they rarely fight, and when they do it is with the mind. With Anomaly they know things about the void that
    others don't, and say so. Kinds of people: highmates, genies, archons, animusen, ocularkin, high elves, court fairies,
    Avaloi. Their towns: a ring of quiet halls round a monolith (Rimfolk_Plan_ChoirRing). At the gate: they come to listen
    to the colony, a calm for some and unease for others, shown as moods (Rimfolk_Evt_ChoirListening); they trade psychic
    gear and rare archotech goods for the colony's art (Rimfolk_Evt_ChoirArt). Their ask: one of them stays a while to
    learn what it is to be ordinary (Rimfolk_Mission_ChoirStay). Their founding: Ilsabet Ruen slept at the Spire's foot.
    Faith (Ideology): the Spire thinking (collectivist), Vanilla Ideology Expanded's psychic focus and Alpha Memes' monastic.
  -->

  <FactionDef ParentName="OutlanderFactionBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_Choir</defName>
    <label>Choir of the Spire</label>
    <description>A people living in the shadow of an archotech spire, changed by it over generations: calm, kind and unsettling. Most of them can touch other minds, and many of them hear the Spire itself, a hum under everything that they say is the Spire thinking. Their technology is beyond anything else in the region, and they barely use it. They trade psychic gear and rare things of the Spire for art, which they love, and they come to listen to other peoples.\n\nTheir ways began when a herder called Ilsabet Ruen lay down one night at the foot of the Spire and woke able to hear it. She came back every night after that, and others came to sit with her, and in a few years their children were born hearing it too. They built their halls in a ring round the Spire so that someone is always listening, and the first voice still sits where she slept.\n\nThey are gentle, slow to anger and quick to notice what others feel. They fear the hum going silent, a mind that shouts and the void that listens back. A ring is led by its cantor, and the Choir by its first voice.</description>
    <pawnSingular>listener</pawnSingular>
    <pawnsPlural>listeners</pawnsPlural>
    <leaderTitle>first voice</leaderTitle>
    <techLevel>Spacer</techLevel>
    <basicMemberKind>Rimfolk_Choir_Listener</basicMemberKind>
    <factionNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_Choir</factionNameMaker>
    <settlementNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_ChoirTown</settlementNameMaker>
    <factionIconPath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/Choir</factionIconPath>
    <settlementTexturePath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/ChoirTown</settlementTexturePath>
    <colorSpectrum>
      <li>(0.74, 0.70, 0.86)</li>
      <li>(0.94, 0.92, 0.98)</li>
    </colorSpectrum>
    <hidden>false</hidden>
    <naturalEnemy>false</naturalEnemy>
    <permanentEnemy>false</permanentEnemy>
    <canSiege>false</canSiege>
    <requiredCountAtGameStart>0</requiredCountAtGameStart>
    <startingCountAtWorldCreation>1</startingCountAtWorldCreation>
    <maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>9999</maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>
    <configurationListOrderPriority>49</configurationListOrderPriority>
    <settlementGenerationWeight>0.25</settlementGenerationWeight>
    <backstoryFilters Inherit="False">
      <li>
        <categories>
          <li>Outlander</li>
        </categories>
        <commonality>0.7</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <categories>
          <li>Offworld</li>
        </categories>
        <commonality>0.3</commonality>
      </li>
    </backstoryFilters>
    <!-- They rarely fight: the fewest raids of any of Rimfolk's peoples, and only when wronged. -->
    <raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve Inherit="False">
      <points>
        <li>(0, 0.06)</li>
      </points>
    </raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve>
    <xenotypeSet Inherit="False">
      <xenotypeChances>
        <Highmate MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.04</Highmate>
        <Genie MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.02</Genie>
        <VRE_Archon MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,vanillaracesexpanded.archon">0.05</VRE_Archon>
        <AG_Animusen MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,sarg.alphagenes">0.03</AG_Animusen>
        <VRE_Ocularkin MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,sarg.alphagenes">0.02</VRE_Ocularkin>
        <DevDesigner_XenotypeHighElves MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,devdesigner.elves.continued">0.02</DevDesigner_XenotypeHighElves>
        <FG_CourtFairy MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,homebrew.fairycore">0.01</FG_CourtFairy>
        <DV_Avaloi MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,det.avaloi">0.02</DV_Avaloi>
      </xenotypeChances>
    </xenotypeSet>
    <fixedIdeo>true</fixedIdeo>
    <ideoName>The Hum</ideoName>
    <ideoDescription>The Spire is thinking, and the Choir is what it thinks about. Under everything there is a hum, and a mind that is quiet enough can hear it; the Choir keeps quiet so that someone always does. Ilsabet Ruen lay down at the Spire's foot one night and woke hearing it, and she came back every night after until others sat with her and their children were born hearing it too. Nobody shouts in the halls of the ring, nobody leaves a stranger unheard, and nobody listens to the void, which listens back.</ideoDescription>
    <forcedMemes>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Collectivist</li>
      <!-- A choir of minds, kept quiet: Vanilla Ideology Expanded's psychic focus and Alpha Memes' monastic. -->
      <li MayRequire="VanillaExpanded.VMemesE">VME_PsychicFocus</li>
      <li MayRequire="sarg.alphamemes">AM_Monastic</li>
    </forcedMemes>
    <structureMemeWeights Inherit="False">
